{
  "summary": "P1 credential phishing. User Aisha Khan (user_id 5, HR Generalist, America/New_York) reports she clicked the link in a 'payroll verification' email and typed her password into the page. She did not give the click time. She didn't mention approving a Duo push or opening an attachment. Checks: account active, not blocked, password last set 2026-09-09. Duo push enrolled. Sign-in logs (last 14 days, 9 entries, newest 2026-10-08 13:35 UTC) are all successful, from New York, US on her usual corporate/residential IPs (203.0.113.10, 198.51.100.25), within usual hours, 0 hosting-network sign-ins, 0 failures or MFA denials. No suspicious activity seen, so block_sign_in NOT requested. The logs have nothing after 2026-10-08, so they may not yet cover the click. Quarantine shows a probable related message: Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain, capital I in place of l), subject 'Urgent: verify your payroll login', received 2026-10-09 09:11 UTC, marked phishing. The email she clicked likely reached her inbox as a copy that got past the filter. Action taken: reset_password queued (approval id 1). Temp password must go by phone after callback verification. Still needed: confirm the click time with the user, re-check sign-ins/Duo pushes after the click, block the sender domain brightIine-help.example org-wide, check whether other users got or clicked the same message, review the mailbox for new inbox rules/forwarding, and consider revoking sessions.",
  "reason": "KB-029 says always escalate. Ticket is P1 credential compromise."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Aisha, thank you for telling us so quickly. That really helps. We're treating your password as stolen, so I've asked for it to be reset and passed this to our security team as a top priority. Once a technician approves the reset, they'll call you to confirm it's you and give you a temporary password over the phone. You'll pick a new one the first time you sign in. We never send passwords by email. In the meantime: 1) Please don't delete the payroll email. Leave it in your mailbox so security can look at it, and don't forward it to anyone. 2) If you used that same password anywhere else, change it there too. 3) If you get a Duo push you didn't start, tap Deny and let us know right away. 4) Please reply with roughly what time you clicked the link, and whether you opened any attachment or approved any Duo prompts. If you opened an attachment, disconnect your laptop from Wi-Fi. So far we haven't seen any unusual sign-ins on your account. The security team will keep watching it.",
  "internal_note": "P1 phishing credential entry per KB-029/KB-008. User 5, active, Duo push enrolled. Sign-in logs: 9 successful sign-ins, all NY/usual IPs/usual hours, no hosting networks, no failures or MFA denials. Newest entry is 2026-10-08, so the logs may not cover the click yet. No suspicious activity, so block_sign_in was not requested. Re-check and block if anything shows up. Quarantine has a related phishing message Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain), 'Urgent: verify your payroll login', 2026-10-09 09:11 UTC. Not releasable and not released. reset_password queued (approval 1): give the temp password by phone after callback verification only. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation 1) for sender block, a check of other recipients, an inbox-rule review, and session revocation. Asked the user for the click time and whether she opened an attachment or approved a Duo push.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-029",
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
